/-!
# VIII08 — the fixed point `Y = 1 + T Y` and `Lmag Y = 0`

`T` is additive on `C⁰[3,∞)` and Lipschitz in the sup norm on `[3, R]`:
`|T g R - T h R| ≤ (R-3) · sup_{[3,R]} |g - h|` (the `3/2` from `t/(t-1)` and the `2/3` from `V` cancel).
The factorial tail of the Picard series therefore makes the partial sums converge to `Y` *and* their images
converge to `T Y`, giving `T Y R = Y R - 1` on `[3, ∞)`.

Consequences proved here:
* `Y_eq_one_add_TY : Y R = 1 + T Y R`.
* `Lmag_Y_eq_zero` (next file, from the derivative identity `P (T h)' = ∫₃^R V h`).
-/

